g the runs.\n\n**What I did**\n- **Measurement script:** `.theseus/oracle/journeys/open-docx-100p.sh` and `open-docx-100p-run.cjs` are a copy of the 10-page runner from PKT-0126, with a different sample and the timeout raised to 240 s. `serve-integrated.sh` already existed, so I didn't write one.\n- **Sample:** `open-docx-100p.docx` is `large-100p.docx` from PKT-0016 (89 KB), copied from the example's file store.\n- **Map:** `.theseus/journeys/open-docx-100p.md` has 12 stages that add up exactly to 4 628 ms, with `unattributed_ms: 0`. The x2t time (243 ms) comes from the converter log.\n\n**Where the time goes, by module**\n\n| module | ms | share |\n|---|---|---|\n| sdkjs-word | 1 723 | 37 % |\n| web-apps-documenteditor | 1 187 | 26 % |\n| project (example service, nginx, browser) | 1 038 | 22 % |\n| sdkjs-common | 264 | 6 % |\n| x2t | 243 | 5 % |\n| docservice | 173 | 4 % |\n\nThe largest single stage is the layout of the remaining pages after `isDocumentLoadComplete`: 1 250 ms, 27 % of the total.\n\n**Decisions**\n- The 1 129 ms between receiving Editor.bin and `isDocumentLoadComplete` is split between modules using the CPU-profile shares PKT-0043 measured earlier. That split is an estimate, not a profile of this run, the same method the 10-page map used. I recorded a follow-up request to measure it properly; it's committed with the work for the factory to approve.\n- The 646 ms Editor.bin download stage is not split into network time and time waiting for the browser's main thread; that needs a trace, and the same follow-up asks for it.\n\n**Surprises**\n- The \"100-page\" sample lays out as 86 pages in this build.\n- This 100-page total (4.6 s) is lower than the 10-page total (8.3 s). That's because PKT-0126 ran with the machine heavily loaded (load average about 6), not because larger files are faster. The stages that depend on document size do grow from 10 to 100 pages: layout after load goes from 741 to 1 250 ms and the Editor.bin stage from 355 to 646 ms. x2t stays flat (299 vs 243 ms).\n\nThe executor log in the packet and my friction line are written.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- sdkjs-word's background page layout is what makes opening slower as documents get bigger.\n- Compare journeys by their shares of the total, not absolute times, unless both ran on a quiet machine.\n- The docx journeys each copy the same runner; a shared runner that takes the sample as a parameter would avoid that.","ttft_ms":2932,"type":"result","duration_ms":190434,"uuid":"36c3c16e-7f1f-47c8-9274-08be88d75b8d","ttft_stream_ms":1808,"time_to_request_ms":318,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":221,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":18,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":5,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":17,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":64,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":136,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":210,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":138,"process_rss_mib_result":230,"process_anon_mib_result":140,"process_peak_rss_mib":243,"process_cpu_ms_turn":3045,"process_wall_ms_turn":190434,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":877,"process_wall_ms_streaming":54698,"main_stream_count":11,"main_stream_event_count":1079,"main_stream_chunk_count":809,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":877,"wall_ms":54698,"entries":11},"tool":{"cpu_ms":1391,"wall_ms":118122,"entries":10},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":439,"wall_ms":17106,"entries":11},"before_first_request":{"cpu_ms":135,"wall_ms":317,"entries":1},"between_requests":{"cpu_ms":194,"wall_ms":182,"entries":10},"after_last_request":{"cpu_ms":9,"wall_ms":9,"entries":1}},"input_attach